      "reason": "The request asks how exercise affects gene expression. The paper's RNA-seq estimand is tomatidine vs vehicle within stimulated myobundles (S2.7.p1, S3.2.p1); stimulation is held constant. Candidate alternatives rejected: (1) trt tomatidine vs vehicle within cohort: analyzable but a pharmacological contrast, not exercise; (2) cohort OS vs YA: donor age/activity status confounded with the single donor cell source, not an exercise intervention, and not a paper DE contrast; (3) tomatidine x cohort interaction: not exercise. Small n is not the reason for stopping.",
      "method": "llm",
      "alternatives": [],
      "evidence_ids": [
        "SRC-0001",
        "ART-0004",
        "ART-0006"
      ],
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "details": {
        "decision_status": "refused",
        "execution_status": "not_started",
        "stop_reason": "No exercise contrast is identifiable. All 12 sequenced myobundles received exercise-like E-Stim (Table 1; GEO treatment field '( EStim)' on every sample); there is no unstimulated or pre-stimulation arm. The data support only tomatidine vs vehicle under E-Stim (a drug effect) and YA vs OS (donor age/activity, one donor source per cohort, aliased with donor), neither of which is an effect of exercise."
      },
